---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { sourceAudit, incidents, href, fmtUsd } from '../lib/data';
import CategoryChip from '../components/CategoryChip.astro';
import { CATEGORIES } from '../lib/taxonomy';
const withAi = incidents.filter((i) => i.ai);
const llama = withAi.filter((i) => i.classifiedBy === 'defillama');
const llamaAgree = llama.filter((i) => i.ai!.category === i.category).length;
const curated = withAi.filter((i) => i.classifiedBy === 'curated');
const curatedAgree = curated.filter((i) => i.ai!.category === i.category).length;
const byTs = incidents.filter((i) => i.classifiedBy === 'typesafe').length;
const replaced = incidents.filter((i) => i.classifiedBy === 'typesafe' && i.classificationNote?.includes('Replaced keyword')).length;
const disagreements = withAi
  .filter((i) => i.ai!.category !== i.category && i.ai!.confidence >= 0.9 && i.ai!.category !== 'unknown')
  .sort((a, b) => (b.amountUsd ?? 0) - (a.amountUsd ?? 0));
const model = withAi[0]?.ai?.model ?? 'jev';
const groups = [...new Set(sourceAudit.map((s) => s.category))];
const NAMES: Record<string, string> = { 'exploit-database': 'Hack & exploit databases', 'vulnerability-dataset': 'Vulnerability datasets', 'protocol-advisories': 'Client, consensus & protocol advisories', 'taxonomy-research': 'Taxonomies & research' };
const count = (s: string) => incidents.filter((i) => i.sources.includes(s as never)).length;
---
<Base title="Sources & method" description="The 30 blockchain-security sources we evaluated, what each provides, and how the index is built.">
  <h1>Sources &amp; method</h1>
  <p class="lede">How the index is built, and an audit of 30 public blockchain-security sources: what each covers, whether it is machine-readable, and how far to trust it.</p>

  <h2>How the index is built</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Backbone: <a href="https://defillama.com/hacks">DefiLlama</a></strong> ({count('defillama')} incidents, 2011 to today). Gives the date, amount, chain, target type and a two-level classification.</li>
    <li><strong>Root causes and PoCs: <a href="https://github.com/SunWeb3Sec/DeFiHackLabs">DeFiHackLabs</a></strong> ({count('defihacklabs')} incidents). Matched by name and date (±7 days), with technical root-cause text and a runnable Foundry exploit. Unmatched entries are added as new incidents.</li>
    <li><strong>Narrative and audit status: <a href="https://rekt.news/">REKT</a></strong> ({count('rekt')} incidents). The leaderboard adds an article link, excerpt and audit status (±10 days).</li>
    <li><strong>More incidents and descriptions:</strong> the <a href="https://defihacklabs.io/explorer/index.html">DeFiHackLabs explorer</a> (detailed root causes, tx hashes), <a href="https://blocksec.com/security-incident">BlockSec</a> ({count('blocksec')}, attack transactions), <a href="https://hacked.slowmist.io/en/">SlowMist</a> ({count('slowmist')}, back to 2012, incl. exchanges, scams and 51% attacks) and <a href="https://revertiq.ai/hacks">RevertIQ</a> ({count('revertiq')}). Each is matched against everything merged before it (name + date, with a strict same-name fallback); unmatched records become new incidents. Third-party text is quoted briefly (≤ 700 characters) with a link back. SlowMist entries it labels <em>Scam</em> or <em>Ponzi</em> (51, e.g. BitConnect, OneCoin) are excluded: they are frauds, not security failures, and would dominate the loss totals.</li>
    <li><strong>Infrastructure:</strong> Bitcoin Core, Geth and Cosmos advisories, plus {count('curated')} hand-curated records: base-layer failures (value overflow, chain splits, outages) and post-mortem root causes for landmark hacks (The DAO, Ronin, Wormhole, Bybit…).</li>
    <li><strong>Classification:</strong> upstream labels are mapped onto our <a href={href('/patterns')}>taxonomy</a>, with documented overrides (e.g. 51% attacks that DefiLlama files as "Forged Proof"). Free-text-only records are classified by TypeSafe (below), falling back to ordered keyword rules. Every record is schema-validated (zod) at build time.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Model classification (TypeSafe)</h2>
  <p>Every incident is also sent to <a href="https://typesafe.ai">TypeSafe</a>'s {model} model: one typed <em>Choice</em> over the {Object.keys(CATEGORIES).length - 1} patterns, plus three yes/no <em>Noul</em> questions (does the text explain the attack, was a flash loan used, is it attributed to a state actor). The model sees the incident's facts and its single most technical description, but not our label.</p>
  <h3>How the questions were chosen</h3>
  <p class="small">We tested designs against human labels (DefiLlama and our curated post-mortems) on a fixed test set of ~250 incidents stratified by pattern, asking all variants in the same request so they saw identical input:</p>
  <ul class="small">
    <li><strong>One description beats many.</strong> Sending every source's account cost 7 points of accuracy; the model works best on a short, focused input.</li>
    <li><strong>Wording mattered less than expected.</strong> Plain definitions, detailed "covers / not for / examples" rubrics, and reversed option order all landed within 2.4 points (78–80% exact, ~87% at the layer level). We kept the cheapest.</li>
    <li><strong>Confidence is the useful signal.</strong> At ≥ 0.9 confidence the model was right ~91% of the time; at 0.7–0.9, 76%. Below 0.7 our keyword rules did better, so the model's answer is adopted only at ≥ 0.7.</li>
    <li><strong>Fixing the taxonomy mattered more than prompting.</strong> Several "errors" were our own mapping contradicting our definitions (e.g. keys stolen from servers filed as infrastructure). Fixing that raised measured agreement by about 3 points.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="grid grid-4">
    <div class="card stat"><div class="value">{Math.round((llamaAgree / Math.max(llama.length, 1)) * 100)}%</div><div class="label">agreement with DefiLlama's human labels ({llamaAgree}/{llama.length})</div></div>
    <div class="card stat"><div class="value">{curatedAgree}/{curated.length}</div><div class="label">agreement with our curated post-mortems</div></div>
    <div class="card stat"><div class="value">{byTs}</div><div class="label">incidents classified by TypeSafe (it replaced {replaced} keyword guesses)</div></div>
    <div class="card stat"><div class="value">{disagreements.length}</div><div class="label">confident disagreements (≥ 0.9) worth reviewing</div></div>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">Policy: the model's answer is adopted only when no human label exists (keyword guesses and unclassified incidents), its confidence is ≥ 0.7, and it judged that the description explains the attack. Human labels are never overwritten; the model's view is shown next to them. Answers are cached in <code>data/typesafe/classifications.json</code> and re-requested only when an incident's text changes.</p>
  {disagreements.length > 0 && (
    <details>
      <summary>Show the {disagreements.length} confident disagreements</summary>
      <div class="table-wrap" style="margin-top:8px">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Incident</th><th>Assigned</th><th>Model says</th><th class="num">Conf.</th><th class="num">Lost</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>{disagreements.map((i) => <tr><td><a href={href(`/hacks/${i.id}`)}>{i.name}</a><div class="small muted">{i.technique}</div></td><td><CategoryChip id={i.category} /></td><td><CategoryChip id={i.ai!.category} /></td><td class="num">{i.ai!.confidence.toFixed(2)}</td><td class="num">{fmtUsd(i.amountUsd)}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </details>
  )}

  <p class="small muted">Amounts are nominal USD at the time of the incident, as reported by the source. Cross-source duplicates are merged with fuzzy name matching, so expect a small number of missed or incorrect merges. Corrections welcome.</p>

  <h2>Source audit</h2>
  {sourceAudit.length === 0 && <p class="muted">Source audit not available.</p>}
  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section>
      <h3>{NAMES[g] ?? g}</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Source</th><th>Status</th><th>Tracks</th><th>Machine-readable</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Concerns</th><th>Priority</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {sourceAudit.filter((s) => s.category === g).map((s) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="mono small">{s.id}</td>
                <td><a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a><div class="small muted">{s.notes}</div></td>
                <td><span class:list={['chip', s.status]}>{s.status}</span></td>
                <td class="small">{s.tracks}</td>
                <td class="small mono" style="overflow-wrap:anywhere;min-width:180px">{s.machineReadable}</td>
                <td class="small">{s.coverage}<div class="muted">{s.chains}</div></td>
                <td class="small">{s.concerns}<div class="muted">License: {s.license}</div></td>
                <td class="num">{'★'.repeat(4 - s.priority)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}
</Base>
<style>
  .chip.offline { color: var(--accent); }
  td { min-width: 110px; }
</style>
